        "original_id": "c833233a-b85c-5f0c-b0e5-39596101f338",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sergio Leone, Jon Paul Puno, Lee Van Cleef, Yul Brynner, George Kennedy\n- Roles: film director, producer, screenwriter, filmmaker, singer, actor\n- Works: For a Few Dollars More, The Magnificent Seven Ride\n- Concepts: Spaghetti Western\n\nFacts:\n- Sergio Leone was born on 3 January 1929 and died on 30 April 1989.\n- Sergio Leone was an Italian film director, producer, and screenwriter.\n- Sergio Leone was credited as the inventor of the Spaghetti Western genre.\n- Lee Van Cleef suffered serious injuries in a car crash.\n- Lee Van Cleef was losing interest in his apparently waning career when Sergio Leone gave him a major role in For a Few Dollars More.\n- Jon Paul Puno was born in 1985.\n- Jon Paul Puno is an American filmmaker and classical crossover singer.\n- The Magnificent Seven Ride stars Lee Van Cleef as Chris Adams.\n- In The Magnificent Seven Ride, Lee Van Cleef succeeded Yul Brynner and George Kennedy in the role of Chris Adams.",
